  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\"><mtable columnalign=\"center left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>if</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>is</mi><mo>odd</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>x</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>if</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>is</mi><mo>even</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> A such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is even then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is odd then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math> we can say that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math> if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is even</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is odd then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> can take any value in set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math></p><p>so number of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>"
